      "writtenOn": "2026-09-23T07:37:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This also breaks the pattern that we register REST API endpoints in dedicated modules, one per REST API namespace. A pattern that makes it easy to find REST API endpoint definitions and how they are wired in Gerrit. I would prefer not to break this.\nThe REST API endpoints available in replicas is a subset of the ones available in primary Gerrits. Thus, we could split the ConfigRestApiModule to represent this instead of using if-condtions all over the place.",
      "revId": "902c21280af673e8e040e87eb0de9bbe1392b151",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
